# Python Code Style Rule

## Baseline

- Target Python: 3.10+
- Follow PEP 8 strictly.
- Keep max line length at 88.

## Type Hints

- Add type hints to all function parameters and return types.
- Avoid untyped public APIs.

## Documentation

- Add Google-style docstrings for all public classes and methods.
- Explain behavioral contract (inputs, outputs, exceptions), not obvious syntax.

## Quality Defaults

- Prefer explicit names over abbreviations.
- Keep functions focused and small.
- Avoid hidden side effects; make state transitions obvious.
